# Monorepo

This repository is an npm workspaces monorepo:

- `apps/backend` — Express + PostgreSQL API (`@ai-workflow/backend`)
- `apps/frontend` — React + Vite SPA (`@ai-workflow/frontend`)

## Commands (run from repo root)

```bash
npm run dev:backend      # API on :3000
npm run dev:frontend     # SPA on :5173 (proxies /api to backend)
npm run typecheck        # all workspaces
npm run lint             # all workspaces
npm run test             # backend integration tests
```

## Boundaries

- Backend owns persistence, auth tokens, and business rules.
- Frontend owns UI state, routing, and API consumption only.
- Shared types live in each app; do not create a shared package unless a human approves it.
- Run quality checks from the repo root before finishing any task.

## Agent customization

- **Rules** (this folder): short, always-on or file-scoped constraints. `agent-skills.mdc`
  routes non-trivial work through `using-agent-skills` first.
- **Skills**: architecture overviews in `apps/<app>/.cursor/skills/`; deep, per-library
  patterns and the `/new-resource` scaffold in the top-level `.cursor/skills/`.
- Repo-wide lifecycle skills (all 24 from
  [addyosmani/agent-skills](https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills)) live in
  `.cursor/skills/` — the source of truth, per upstream's own `docs/cursor-setup.md`.
  Their supporting checklists live in `.cursor/references/` and specialist review
  personas in `.cursor/agents/` — both synced from upstream `references/`/`agents/` 1:1,
  so a skill file's relative mention of `references/x.md` or `agents/x.md` resolves
  there. `agent-skills/` is a pinned git submodule (upstream vendor copy) — update it
  with `git submodule update --remote` and `rsync` into these three folders (see
  README) — the `npx skills` CLI writes to `.agents/skills/`, not `.cursor/skills/`, so
  it can't manage this tree; `skills-lock.json` records the last synced state.
- The 8 lifecycle commands (`/spec /plan /build /test /review /code-simplify /webperf
  /ship`) live in `.cursor/skills/<command>/` as `disable-model-invocation` skills, since
  Cursor has no native slash-command or subagent primitive — see
  `docs/agentic-engineering-workflow.md` for the full phase diagram.
- There is no `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` — this rules + skills setup is the single source
  of truth for both humans and agents.

See [Cursor Rules](https://cursor.com/docs/rules.md) and [Agent Skills](https://cursor.com/docs/skills.md).
